# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
import { createApp, defineComponent } from "vue";

defineComponent({
  model: {
    prop: "value",
    event: "input",
  },
});

defineComponent((props) => {}, {
  model: {},
});

createApp({
  model: ({
    event: "change",
  }),
});

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-component-forms.js:5:3 lint/nursery/noVueDeprecatedModelDefinition ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The model option is deprecated.
  
     4 │ defineComponent({
   > 5 │   model: {
       │   ^^^^^^^^
   > 6 │     prop: "value",
   > 7 │     event: "input",
   > 8 │   },
       │   ^
     9 │ });
    10 │ 
  
  i Vue 3 ignores this option. v-model on a component always uses the modelValue prop and the update:modelValue event.
  
  i Rename the prop to modelValue and emit update:modelValue, or keep the prop name and use a named v-model such as v-model:checked. See the Vue 3 migration guide for more information.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

